TI  - Treatment of infection associated with tunneled pleural catheters.
PG  - 69-72
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3181ca66c1 [doi]
AB  - Chronic indwelling tunneled pleural catheters are increasingly used for the 
      treatment of malignant pleural effusions. Some common complications of these 
      catheters include empyema and local site infection. Empyema is generally treated 
      with the removal of the pleural catheter and the administration of systemic 
      antibiotics. We propose a different and more conservative but effective method of 
      the treatment of infected tunneled pleural catheters.
